.SH NAME
filecrypt \- encrypt and decrypt files

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filecrypt
.BR \-e | \-d
.BI \-i " input"
.BI \-o " output"
.RB [ \-k " key-file" ]
.RB [ \-f ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filecrypt
encrypts and decrypts files using AES-256-GCM encryption.

If no key file is provided, the program asks the user to enter a password.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-encrypt
Encrypt the input file.

.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-decrypt
Decrypt the input file.

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-input " FILE"
Specify the input file.

.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Specify the output file.

.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key-file " FILE"
Read the password from a file.

.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Replace an existing output file.

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information.

.SH EXAMPLES

Encrypt a file:

.EX
filecrypt -e -i message.txt -o message.fc
.EE

Decrypt a file:

.EX
filecrypt -d -i message.fc -o recovered.txt
.EE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
The operation completed successfully.

.TP
.B 1
An error occurred.

.SH SECURITY
Passwords and encryption keys are erased from memory after use.

An incorrect password or modified encrypted file causes decryption to fail.

